---
functor: 1
title: Document settings
---

set heading(numbering: none)

Four rules set the look of the whole page. The rules for math kinds are on [Grids, matrices, vectors, cases](structures/grids.html) and [Fences and wrap](structures/fences.html). The full list is on [All set rules](document/set-rules.html).

```fn
set document(style: classic, accent: #4a6a85)
set heading(numbering: none, new_page: 1)
set page(size: a5, margin: 2cm)
set text(size: 10pt, font: "Functor LM")
```

# document

| Option | Values | Result |
|:--|:--|:--|
| `style` | `quiet` (default), `classic`, `lecture`, `compact`, `board` | `quiet`: the title at the left, numbers in the margin, upright theorems with a rule, notes in the right margin. `classic`: the LaTeX article look. `lecture`: notes in the left margin, § before section numbers, theorems on a tinted band. `compact`: two columns on wide pages, an indent on each paragraph that follows a paragraph, notes after the paragraph. `board`: a dark page with larger type and light labels, for a projector. The HTML and the PDF use the same style. |
| `accent` | a hex colour, for example `#4a6a85` | the colour of numbers and rules |

# heading

| Option | Values | Result |
|:--|:--|:--|
| `numbering` | `none` | removes the numbers from headings |
| `new_page` | `none` (default), or a level from `1` to `6` | each heading of that level or a higher level starts a new page. `new_page: 1` breaks at each `#` heading. See [Page breaks](document/parts.html). |

# page

| Option | Values |
|:--|:--|
| `size` | `a4` (default), `a5`, `letter` |
| `margin` | a length: `2.5cm`, `20mm`, `1in`, `72pt` |

# text

| Option | Values |
|:--|:--|
| `size` | a length, for example `11pt` |
| `font` | a font name in quotes |

A length is a number and a unit: `pt`, `mm`, `cm`, `in` or `em`.
